Under primitiveUnits=“objectBoundingBox”, Ladybird scales a primitive’s
horizontal lengths by the bounding box’s width and its vertical ones by
its height. Chrome 157, Firefox 151 and WebKit (Playwright’s 26.5 build)
do the same, verified at runtime with the new test. Blink’s
Filter::ApplyHorizontalScale() and ApplyVerticalScale() scale by the
reference box under kBoundingBox, and its FEDisplacementMap takes the
horizontal scale for its single Skia factor too.
